From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Mark the assertion-only locals of physical_iejoin.cpp as used

physical_iejoin.cpp declares locals that only D_ASSERT() reads (op),
so in a release build, where D_ASSERT() expands to nothing, they are unused
and -Wunused-variable or -Wunused-but-set-variable says so. Each is cast
to void after its declaration, which changes no behavior.

Carried here until upstream takes it; not proposed upstream yet.

---
diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/execution/operator/join/physical_iejoin.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/execution/operator/join/physical_iejoin.cpp
--- a/src/duckdb/src/execution/operator/join/physical_iejoin.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/execution/operator/join/physical_iejoin.cpp
@@ -1418,6 +1418,7 @@ void IEJoinLocalSourceState::SplitPayloads(DataChunk &chunk) {
 const SelectionVector *IEJoinLocalSourceState::ApplyArbitraryPredicate(DataChunk &chunk) {
 	//	Apply any arbitrary predicate
 	auto &op = gsource.op;
+	(void)op;
 	D_ASSERT(op.predicate);
 
 	const auto result_count = pred_executor.SelectExpression(chunk, pred_matches);
